{number: 71}
{title: Something for Thee}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] Savior, Thy dying love Thou gavest [D7] me,
Nor should I [G] aught withhold, [C] dear Lord, from [G] Thee:
In love my [C] soul would bow, my heart ful-[G] fill its vow,
Some off'ring [D7] bring Thee now, something for [G] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
At [G] the blest mercy seat, pleading for [D7] me,
My feeble [G] faith looks up, [C] Jesus, to [G] Thee:
Help me the [C] cross to bear, Thy wondrous [G] love declare,
Some song to [D7] raise, or prayer, something for [G] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Give [G] me a faithful heart, likeness to [D7] Thee,
That each de-[G] parting day [C] henceforth may [G] see
Some work of [C] love begun, some deed of [G] kindness done,
Some wand'rer [D7] sought and won, something for [G] Thee.
{end_of_verse}
